 :design {:representation "Pure bounded, single-grant simulated trace reduction over explicit input data; at most 64 events. The trace is a transient test value, not a ledger, persistent store, authority, or new parser. Use existing closed shape checks, transcript, binding, resource-byte and clock predicates; do not duplicate those contracts. Unknown/malformed/improper/cyclic inputs deny, with bounded traversal and no mutation."
          :ownership "The caller supplies all synthetic records, time, storage outcomes and event sequence; none becomes a real owner fact. Do not accept a caller-provided grant state or counts as authoritative. Construct one fresh model state from the first issue event and reduce subsequent events in sequence. No global variables, callbacks or ambient I/O."
          :history-limit "A repeated consume/final event within the same complete simulated trace is denied after terminal state. A caller can submit an older trace or fork/replay the whole input: a pure function without an external owner cannot detect that. Do not claim cross-invocation replay prevention, simultaneity, real revocation or persistence."
          :immutability "At issue copy the validated exact transcript, digest, identity, approval, grant, release, contract pin and synthetic resource bytes. Derive and copy operation, grant ID and deadlines from those records. At consume and final compare presented records and invocation against the snapshot with existing issue/final binding checks; verify bytes AND digest, pin, grant ID, resource, channel binding and all records. The only existing synthetic session/channel binding is identity channel-binding: do not invent operator-session authentication. For read, bind the entire release record including destination, policy scope and policy generation; contract pin remains distinct from release-record binding."
          :deadlines "Derive ordered deadline vector from copied identity credential-not-after, approval not-after, grant not-after and, for read only, release not-after. Check issued-at relationships and all safe integers. Validate the issue sample using strict latest < each deadline; bound requested grant/approval validity to the reviewed issuance rule, including latest+60000 capped safely, and derive monotonic deadline once as issue monotonic + (minimum deadline - issue latest), rejecting overflow. Never accept a later replacement deadline or independently supplied monotonic deadline as authority. Earlier or changed record values are substitutions and deny rather than silently rebind."
          :phases "Issue -> consume -> final, with explicit synthetic owner-order and count fields inside reducer state. Check copied binding, grant ID, status and fresh clock at issue and consume; simulate successful consume before any modeled effect. Recheck exact binding, record-derived UTC deadlines and monotonic deadline after storage outcome at final, then simulate a final gap with the existing clock model. Final denial, restart or ticket loss after consume keeps consumed terminal; expiry before consume invalidates. Revoke before consume yields revoked; after consume reports already-consumed; invalidated revoke yields unavailable, never ACK. Storage failure or uncertainty denies with no modeled effects and must not manufacture a durable result. Issue/revoke/consume/final events are separate finite model events, not owner operations."
          :counts "Model read success increments only simulated bytes by end-start from the bound invocation; write success increments only simulated mutation entries by one. Denials have zero increments. Neither count is evidence of a native mutation, plaintext transfer, durability or atomicity."}
 :proposed-apis [{:name "oikos-owner-model-composed-run" :file "layers/agent-sandbox/oikos-owner-authority.el"
                  :signature "(events) -> closed synthetic result or fixed denial"
                  :contract "Total bounded reducer: first and only issue, known event variants with exact keys; validate before dereference/copy, reject repeated grant issue, duplicate/unknown keys and malformed or cyclic top-level and nested values. Return copied final state/result and per-event synthetic outcome/order; no caller initial state. Accept only bound inputs explicitly included in each phase and use returned reducer state for the next event."}
                 {:name "oikos-owner-model--composed-issue" :file "layers/agent-sandbox/oikos-owner-authority.el"
                  :signature "(issue-event) -> copied synthetic snapshot/state or denial"
                  :contract "Delegate to existing invocation/record validators and oikos-owner-model-issue; derive deadlines and monotonic bound from the valid records and issue clock, safe arithmetic, exact read/write scope; never mint real grants."}
                 {:name "oikos-owner-model--composed-step" :file "layers/agent-sandbox/oikos-owner-authority.el"
                  :signature "(state event) -> new synthetic state/outcome"
                  :contract "Internal to one reducer invocation; explicit consume/final/revoke/restart transitions and strict binding/deadline checks. Reuse existing clock and final comparison; do not expose an alternative path that treats arbitrary caller state as owner fact."}
                 {:name "oikos-owner-model-test--composed-fixture" :file "tests/unit/oikos-owner-authority-test.el"
