                  :contract "Build independent copied read/write inputs from existing fixture helpers with distinct record deadlines, avoiding shared literal mutation; expected counts and order are explicit."}]
 :finite-red-oracles
 [{:id :positive-and-replay :cases "For read and write issue/consume/final while fresh; assert exact returned order, operation, grant ID and increments; append duplicate consume/final events to the same complete trace and assert denial and unchanged counts. Assert the reducer's output is not an owner token; do not assert replay resistance when the entire trace is resubmitted."}
  {:id :binding-swaps :cases "At consume and separately at final change grant ID, same-actor credential ID, actor/entity, actor or credential generation, channel/session binding, epoch/incarnation/revision, synthetic bytes or range, contract pin, read destination, release policy scope/generation, and replacement. Assert denial, zero new counts and exact terminal state; include mutating original inputs after issue to test copied snapshot. A changed approval/identity/grant/release deadline or digest also denies, even if still future."}
  {:id :deadlines :cases "Use distinct credential, approval, grant and read policy deadlines. Independently reach strict equality and expiry at each applicable bound, plus monotonic equality, at issue/consume/final. Read and write expiry after successful consume stays consumed with zero count; include post-final-check expiry gap and unexpired controls. Caller-supplied forged larger deadlines or altered derived monotonic bound are not accepted as inputs."}
  {:id :revocation-and-order :cases "Both operations: revoke before consume -> revoked then consume denied; consume then revoke -> already-consumed and no extra effect; restart before consume -> invalidated and unavailable revoke; restart after consume -> consumed and no final effect. Feed returned internal trace state sequentially; assert exact order/counts, no simulated durable ACK after storage failure/uncertainty."}
  {:id :closed-totality :cases "Bounded table across trace, event, record, snapshot and clock inputs: nil, scalar, improper and cyclic lists, duplicate/unknown/missing keys, wrong operation, over-limit events, unsafe integer and malformed text. Assert fixed denial, termination and no input mutation, with valid positive control. Snapshot cycles must not reach unbounded copy/equal; validate bounded acyclic structure before walking it."}
  {:id :translated-prior-overflow :cases "Let M=9007199254740991. Prior=(M-10,10,10,t), current=(M-10,0,11,t), UTC deadline=(M), monotonic deadline=30: current latest < M, prior upper = M, monotonic advances one and UTC lower does not regress, but translated prior upper = M+1; assert denial specifically for translated bound overflow. Add a nearby non-overflow positive where translated interval overlaps and all earlier guards pass."}
  {:id :copy-and-storage :cases "Per operation mutate the caller-owned input after constructing the model issue snapshot in a controlled fixture; exact copied snapshot remains unchanged and changed final record denies. Exercise failed and uncertain storage as separate cases, no effect/release, no successful revoke ACK, and no automatic retry."}]
